    "alert_id": "P005_TDF_RENAL_DECLINE_001",
    "title": "Progressive renal impairment on TDF with rising creatinine",
    "message": "Guidelines list chronic kidney disease and Fanconi syndrome as major TDF toxicities, requiring serum creatinine and eGFR monitoring. Patient's creatinine has risen steadily from 0.9 (2020) to 1.4 mg/dL over 3 years on TDF, with eGFR now 52 mL/min/1.73m2 and proteinuria 1+ — a consistent worsening trend consistent with TDF nephrotoxicity. Evidence for drug attribution: temporal relationship with TDF initiation, progressive decline, and proteinuria. Evidence against: no oedema, stable weight, normal BP, and no documented Fanconi features (glycosuria is only trace); non-drug causes should still be excluded. No clinician plan was documented today.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Repeat creatinine/eGFR and urinalysis to confirm trend; evaluate non-drug causes; consider switching TDF to TAF or alternative backbone per guidelines if decline confirmed.",
