    "alert_id": "P005_IBUPROFEN_TDF_INTERACTION_003",
    "title": "Frequent ibuprofen use compounds TDF renal risk",
    "message": "Guidelines identify chronic kidney disease and acute kidney injury as major TDF adverse events. The patient takes ibuprofen 400mg 2-3 times weekly for 6 months, and NSAIDs are nephrotoxic, compounding TDF's renal tubular effects — particularly concerning given her eGFR of 52 and proteinuria. This is a compounding risk: TDF plus regular NSAID use plus existing renal impairment. Her headaches, noted as a TDF toxicity symptom in guidelines, may also warrant drug review.",
    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Counsel patient to stop or minimise ibuprofen use; recommend paracetamol for headaches; reassess renal function after NSAID discontinuation.",
