      {"page_number": 37, "chunk_id": "hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__hiv_guidelines_art.extraction__p37_c1"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "alert_id": "P005_NO_PLAN_DOCUMENTED_004",
    "title": "No assessment or plan documented despite abnormal renal labs",
    "message": "Guidelines require clinicians to monitor for TDF toxicity signs and perform renal function tests, with management actions if deranged. Today's encounter shows no written assessment or plan despite creatinine of 1.4 mg/dL, eGFR 52, and proteinuria 1+ on a TDF-containing regimen. The patient's fatigue and headaches are listed TDF toxicity symptoms that were not addressed. Viral suppression is excellent (VL <50, CD4 584), so ART efficacy is not a concern.",
    "issue_type": "plan_review",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Document assessment addressing renal decline, fatigue, and headaches; order repeat renal labs; consider TDF toxicity evaluation and regimen review.",
